WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.078
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:29.348 --> 00:30.474
Jorge.

3
00:30.475 --> 00:32.934
I showed the photo to my mom earlier.

4
00:32.935 --> 00:34.102
What did she say?

5
00:34.103 --> 00:36.272
Primitivo Pascual is his name.

6
00:37.356 --> 00:41.527
The one on the photo is my grandfather.

7
00:44.280 --> 00:45.073
Let's go?

8
00:45.074 --> 00:46.074
Let's go.

9
00:52.914 --> 00:54.040
Let me.

10
01:07.136 --> 01:08.804
Hold on tight.

11
01:08.805 --> 01:10.056
Again?

12
01:36.000 --> 01:41.000
"All the Things I Leave You" (Episode 5)

13
01:48.058 --> 01:50.810
I was looking through the letters last night.

14
01:52.479 --> 01:53.854
Did you read them?

15
01:53.855 --> 01:55.273
Not yet.

16
01:57.776 --> 02:01.780
I spent time analyzing the post stamps and dates.

17
02:08.954 --> 02:12.873
There are different kinds of letters.

18
02:12.874 --> 02:15.209
Some are for his mother.

19
02:15.210 --> 02:17.671
The others are for your grandpa.

20
02:21.675 --> 02:25.010
From Hawaii to Ilocos.

21
02:25.011 --> 02:27.096
But Kiko, look.

22
02:27.097 --> 02:29.556
It's like they haven't been read.

23
02:29.557 --> 02:30.599
They're unopened.

24
02:30.600 --> 02:32.644
Huh?

25
02:34.854 --> 02:36.898
And this one.

26
02:38.191 --> 02:40.652
It's from your grandpa.

27
02:41.861 --> 02:44.488
From Ilocos to Hawaii.

28
02:44.489 --> 02:46.031
It hasn't been read?

29
02:46.032 --> 02:47.658
Not only that.

30
02:47.659 --> 02:49.869
It wasn't sent.

31
02:51.413 --> 02:54.207
It never left the country.

32
02:54.958 --> 02:57.877
If it wasn't sent...

33
03:00.005 --> 03:03.133
Then why is it with Grandpa Tino?

34
03:05.969 --> 03:07.804
I have a feeling...

35
03:09.556 --> 03:12.474
It was held back.

36
03:12.475 --> 03:14.310
Oh no.

37
03:17.897 --> 03:21.067
Our grandfathers were writing to each other.

38
03:22.193 --> 03:23.736
But Kiko.

39
03:23.737 --> 03:26.364
Someone held them back.

40
03:28.950 --> 03:30.325
Let's read it now.

41
03:30.326 --> 03:31.326
Can we?

42
03:31.327 --> 03:32.746
Be patient.

43
03:34.789 --> 03:38.043
Let me just organize them.

44
03:40.920 --> 03:42.547
Just one.

45
03:43.298 --> 03:44.674
No.

46
04:07.739 --> 04:08.864
Mother.

47
04:08.865 --> 04:11.158
How are things in Ilocos?

48
04:11.159 --> 04:13.411
It's so different here in Hawaii.

49
04:33.014 --> 04:35.391
Gather ‘round!

50
04:59.833 --> 05:02.960
Were you promoted?

51
05:02.961 --> 05:06.004
This is harder.

52
05:06.005 --> 05:10.802
I can only rest when I fetch water.

53
05:25.066 --> 05:28.402
I want to go back to the Philippines.

54
05:28.403 --> 05:30.445
Are you crazy?

55
05:30.446 --> 05:34.450
What kind of life is waiting for us there after the war?

56
05:41.082 --> 05:43.585
One more?

57
06:24.125 --> 06:26.543
Did you write everything I said?

58
06:26.544 --> 06:27.420
Yes.

59
06:27.421 --> 06:29.922
Did you start with the magazine I gave you?

60
06:29.923 --> 06:32.424
You can learn how to read and write.

61
06:32.425 --> 06:35.845
It's important for the future.

62
06:36.888 --> 06:39.264
Are you complaining?

63
06:39.265 --> 06:41.726
That's not what I mean, Tino.

64
06:42.227 --> 06:44.562
I just care for you.

65
06:48.566 --> 06:51.318
I already told you, Pablo.

66
06:51.319 --> 06:54.530
There's someone waiting for me in San Nicolas.

67
07:01.788 --> 07:03.915
If Bong was here...

68
07:05.833 --> 07:09.003
He would know how to read and write.

69
07:09.671 --> 07:12.465
That's the reason he was not hired here.

70
07:15.301 --> 07:20.013
They rejected the applications of anyone who can read and write.

71
07:20.014 --> 07:22.016
What about you, Pablo?

72
07:22.725 --> 07:23.934
I'm smart.

73
07:23.935 --> 07:26.061
I didn't tell them that I know how to read and write.

74
07:26.062 --> 07:28.231
I acted like an idiot.

75
07:29.148 --> 07:30.650
Is that it?

76
07:32.068 --> 07:34.320
I'm an idiot?

77
07:34.946 --> 07:36.280
That's not what I meant.

78
07:36.281 --> 07:39.574
They just don't want smart people to come here.

79
07:39.575 --> 07:42.495
Because they think we might start a union.

80
07:44.539 --> 07:47.582
Those who know how to read and write

81
07:47.583 --> 07:49.502
have higher positions.

82
07:52.630 --> 07:54.215
Teach me, Pablo.

83
07:55.049 --> 07:56.508
It's up to you.

84
07:56.509 --> 07:57.509
You try.

85
07:57.510 --> 07:59.553
Me, I'm okay with my position now.

86
07:59.554 --> 08:01.763
Better than to risk getting fired.

87
08:01.764 --> 08:03.181
I'll earn for now.

88
08:03.182 --> 08:04.976
Then I'll return home.

89
08:06.686 --> 08:09.063
That's also what I said to Bong.

90
08:10.106 --> 08:13.191
He's waiting for me in San Nicolas.

91
08:13.192 --> 08:15.402
I know, I know.

92
08:15.403 --> 08:17.697
I get it that you love Bong.

93
08:19.866 --> 08:22.368
What was I going to write next?

94
08:26.372 --> 08:28.124
Put...

95
08:30.376 --> 08:32.420
I am just here.

96
08:34.547 --> 08:36.591
I am not giving up.

97
08:49.187 --> 08:52.147
I had no idea

98
08:52.148 --> 08:54.942
that life in Hawaii was that hard.

99
08:58.154 --> 09:01.449
And they said life was good there.

100
09:02.325 --> 09:06.411
I never thought

101
09:06.412 --> 09:09.248
it would be hard like that.

102
09:17.673 --> 09:19.884
One more.

103
09:48.079 --> 09:49.080
Hand.

104
09:51.207 --> 09:52.750
How old are you?

105
09:55.962 --> 09:57.046
Are you a farmer?

106
09:58.423 --> 10:01.759
How old are you again?

107
10:03.344 --> 10:04.846
Where are you from?

108
10:05.930 --> 10:08.306
Do you have relatives in Hawaii?

109
10:08.307 --> 10:09.975
Tino!

110
10:09.976 --> 10:12.436
What took you so long?

111
10:12.437 --> 10:14.564
I had to tell my mother first.

112
10:15.273 --> 10:16.356
Here.

113
10:16.357 --> 10:18.608
Empanada.

114
10:18.609 --> 10:20.862
Don't be angry at me.

115
10:23.197 --> 10:24.782
Get in line.

116
10:26.576 --> 10:29.203
I already registered our names.

117
10:31.330 --> 10:32.706
Bong.

118
10:32.707 --> 10:36.544
They inspect the hands of those who register.

119
10:49.765 --> 10:52.559
What are you looking for there?

120
10:52.560 --> 10:54.103
Wait.

121
10:56.814 --> 10:59.567
There are no rocks there.

122
11:00.485 --> 11:01.776
There are.

123
11:01.777 --> 11:03.070
Just wait.

124
11:18.169 --> 11:19.879
Do as I do.

125
11:20.922 --> 11:22.673
What is this for?

126
11:24.926 --> 11:28.762
We need to make sure our hands are rough.

127
11:28.763 --> 11:33.475
So they will accept us.

128
11:33.476 --> 11:35.603
Where did you learn that?

129
11:39.482 --> 11:41.526
Just do it.

130
11:42.777 --> 11:44.111
Do it.

131
11:46.322 --> 11:47.698
Like this?

132
11:49.116 --> 11:51.868
Not like that, Bong.

133
11:51.869 --> 11:53.913
Do it harder.

134
11:54.413 --> 11:56.666
Let me do it.

135
12:22.108 --> 12:23.775
Why?

136
12:23.776 --> 12:25.570
Does it hurt?

137
12:29.448 --> 12:30.908
No.

138
12:49.969 --> 12:52.138
Are you happy?

139
12:53.973 --> 12:59.061
Imagine our lives in Hawaii.

140
13:00.646 --> 13:02.397
Bong.

141
13:02.398 --> 13:06.943
We could buy our own land when we are there.

142
13:06.944 --> 13:09.404
We can start a business.

143
13:09.405 --> 13:11.907
We will be together.

144
13:13.659 --> 13:16.120
Why does it seem like...

145
13:17.728 --> 13:20.773
you're having second thoughts?

146
13:22.918 --> 13:24.712
Bong.

147
13:25.630 --> 13:28.424
This is for our future.

148
13:34.722 --> 13:37.433
It is not that, Tino.

149
13:40.436 --> 13:42.605
I have a bad feeling.

150
13:46.025 --> 13:48.818
The American seemed mad

151
13:48.819 --> 13:52.823
when he found out I could write and speak English.

152
13:53.866 --> 13:56.535
He seemed alright to me.

153
14:01.457 --> 14:03.917
Bong.

154
14:03.918 --> 14:06.337
Whatever happens,

155
14:08.005 --> 14:10.340
we will not be separated.

156
14:10.341 --> 14:12.677
Okay?

157
14:18.140 --> 14:20.351
Let's go.

158
14:29.318 --> 14:30.568
Put that back.

159
14:30.569 --> 14:32.570
Put them back.

160
14:32.571 --> 14:33.863
Mother.

161
14:33.864 --> 14:35.615
I am not going.

162
14:35.616 --> 14:37.784
Just because Bong was not accepted,

163
14:37.785 --> 14:39.119
you won't go anymore?

164
14:39.120 --> 14:42.455
There are a lot of people who yearn for the glory of Hawaii.

165
14:42.456 --> 14:45.126
You are wasting your chance.

166
14:45.751 --> 14:47.252
Mother...

167
14:47.253 --> 14:50.965
Bong and I promised that we will go together.

168
14:59.140 --> 15:00.974
Listen to me.

169
15:00.975 --> 15:02.726
Do this.

170
15:02.727 --> 15:04.269
For our family.

171
15:04.270 --> 15:06.354
Not for Bong.

172
15:06.355 --> 15:07.939
For you.

173
15:07.940 --> 15:11.527
When you have earned enough, you can come back home.

174
15:25.458 --> 15:28.418
I will find a way to write.

175
15:28.419 --> 15:31.213
Thank you, my child.

176
15:33.382 --> 15:34.716
Mother.

177
15:34.717 --> 15:36.926
For Bong.

178
15:36.927 --> 15:38.261
Not just for you.

179
15:38.262 --> 15:41.015
For Bong, too.

180
15:41.932 --> 15:43.892
I will see to it.

181
15:43.893 --> 15:49.439
I will tell his Grandma Victoria who works at the post office.

182
15:49.440 --> 15:54.153
I will tell her that you will send letters.

183
15:57.031 --> 15:59.324
Mother.

184
15:59.325 --> 16:01.826
Bong, too...

185
16:01.827 --> 16:04.954
He will be sending letters.

186
16:04.955 --> 16:08.666
If he tells you to come back,

187
16:08.667 --> 16:10.001
do not listen to him.

188
16:10.002 --> 16:13.255
I will not be able to resist him.

189
16:15.049 --> 16:17.801
I am sure...

190
16:17.802 --> 16:20.094
He will be writing.

191
16:20.095 --> 16:25.141
I will personally get it and mail to the post office.

192
16:25.142 --> 16:29.020
There will come a day

193
16:29.021 --> 16:33.567
when you will not regret your decision.

194
16:58.008 --> 16:59.342
Jorge.

195
16:59.343 --> 17:01.553
The letter will get wet.

196
17:01.554 --> 17:03.388
Take it. I want to stop.

197
17:03.389 --> 17:04.681
Huh?

198
17:04.682 --> 17:07.268
I don't want to read anymore.

199
17:09.645 --> 17:11.105
Okay.

200
17:13.482 --> 17:15.568
Let's go for a drink?

201
17:17.820 --> 17:21.407
I wanted to read this one.

202
17:22.950 --> 17:25.159
The last letter.

203
17:25.160 --> 17:27.120
But okay...

204
17:27.121 --> 17:29.790
We can read it next time.

205
17:39.550 --> 17:43.971
Let's do it. Now or never.

206
17:59.195 --> 18:03.449
You read it.

207
18:28.182 --> 18:31.810
My beloved Bong,

208
18:32.768 --> 18:37.772
do you still remember the day we applied for Hawaii?

209
18:37.816 --> 18:41.904
We were so happy.

210
19:32.287 --> 19:33.287
Let's go!

211
19:33.288 --> 19:36.249
We don't want to be late at the funeral home.

212
19:36.250 --> 19:39.585
Did you find your mom's favorite dress?

213
19:39.586 --> 19:41.421
Yes, wait.

214
19:41.422 --> 19:42.798
I'm coming.

215
21:23.732 --> 21:28.569
When will you tell your family?

216
21:28.570 --> 21:30.488
About what?

217
21:30.489 --> 21:33.283
About the letters.

218
21:34.284 --> 21:36.661
I won't tell them.

219
21:36.662 --> 21:38.372
Why not?

220
21:40.249 --> 21:43.544
They won't understand it.

221
21:44.211 --> 21:48.382
They have the right to know, Jorge.

222
21:50.801 --> 21:55.389
I don't want Grandpa Tino's name to be tainted.

223
21:57.349 --> 22:02.146
Why, did he do anything wrong?

224
22:07.526 --> 22:13.781
It's better they remember him in death

225
22:13.782 --> 22:17.286
as how they knew him when he was alive.

226
22:18.996 --> 22:20.830
Jorge.

227
22:20.831 --> 22:23.208
That's history.

228
22:23.667 --> 22:29.213
We should never forget.

229
22:29.214 --> 22:32.551
You act like you're not Filipino, Kiko.

230
22:33.177 --> 22:38.891
Filipinos have selective memory.

231
22:39.235 --> 22:42.614
They want good vibes all the time.

232
22:44.605 --> 22:45.771
Why?

233
22:45.772 --> 22:48.649
Grandpa Tino had a happy life.

234
22:48.650 --> 22:50.194
Happy?

235
22:50.736 --> 22:52.195
They separated.

236
22:52.196 --> 22:55.866
And they never saw each other again.

237
22:58.243 --> 23:02.080
- There were happy moments. - What's happy about that?

238
23:03.040 --> 23:05.167
There were happy moments.

239
23:05.667 --> 23:07.294
When they were together.

240
23:12.216 --> 23:13.467
Kiko.

241
23:14.092 --> 23:18.472
Where is your Grandpa Bong?

242
23:19.973 --> 23:21.849
He's dead.

243
23:21.850 --> 23:23.393
How did he die?

244
23:24.811 --> 23:26.104
He was killed.

245
23:29.816 --> 23:32.319
My mom said...

246
23:34.613 --> 23:38.575
Grandpa was a leader of the farmers back then.

247
23:39.243 --> 23:43.331
They fought those who stole their lands.

248
23:43.885 --> 23:45.803
That's why...

249
23:45.827 --> 23:47.330
they shot him.

250
23:47.354 --> 23:50.649
But that was a long time ago.

251
23:55.133 --> 24:00.472
I think when they didn't hear from each other,

252
24:02.683 --> 24:05.560
they married other people.

253
24:06.828 --> 24:08.579
Maybe.

254
24:08.734 --> 24:10.985
Then...

255
24:11.066 --> 24:14.777
Grandpa Bong moved to Cagayan

256
24:14.778 --> 24:20.491
when his application to Hawaii was rejected.

257
24:20.492 --> 24:22.703
We're not like you, Jorge.

258
24:23.537 --> 24:26.373
We didn't become rich.

259
24:45.475 --> 24:46.642
Hello, Auntie.

260
24:46.643 --> 24:50.646
Kiko, a letter arrived for you.

261
24:50.647 --> 24:53.607
I couldn't resist opening it.

262
24:53.608 --> 24:55.818
You passed your scholarship.

263
24:55.819 --> 24:58.863
- Jorge, I passed. - Come home quick!

264
24:58.864 --> 24:59.864
Bye!

265
25:41.031 --> 25:43.241
Tino.
